66)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7441:    used under D439.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7443:- **Decided, citing D439:** two diagnostic accounts at about $0.002 under a $0.02 ceiling. Each is asked neutrally which instruction\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7448:## D579 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the refusal accounts read; no A2 rule yet; a bounded $0 audit of the decline rules and the outcome's extra parts first (council consensus, round 67)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7458:- **Decided, citing D439:** a bounded $0 audit.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7467:## D580 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: no reviewed repair for the unlisted parts; arm A stays stopped; next, a $0 check of the Idea planner on new-system answer shapes (council consensus, rounds 68 and 69)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7481:- **Decided, citing D439:** next, at $0, a check of the Idea planner against stored new-system answers. A stored event, an undirected\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7487:## D581 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the event-driver design parked as recorded input; paid work and new lines held until Alex returns or the council names a gate-moving candidate (council consensus, rounds 70 to 72)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7502:  procedure is not established as a choice only Alex can make (D439); no general candidate has survived review. Deck 1 and the six\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7504:- **Decided, citing D439:** hold paid work and new lines. Keep the records and Alex's page current. Resume on Alex's return or when the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7528:- **Decided, citing D439 and Alex's instruction:** send A2's probe and read it as designed.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7537:  - Spend $0.15; D439 about $26.33 of $40 used.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7544:- **Why** (D439, D583): A2's one harm traced to the change is over-listing: an event's own outcomes listed as not judged. The model's\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7572:  readings and both countings. Spend $0.2204; D439 about $26.55 of $40 used.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7630:  largest charge was $0.033). D439 spend is about