$0 under D439; do not\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8613:  overrides nothing. Then a council decision under D439 records it as reversible, and a request audit follows before a probe.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8671:**The probe** (`reflection-6/due-day/RESULT.md`, $1.71; D439 about $36.4 of $40):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8727:- **Arms and cap:** 10 exposed topics outside the 44, 2 interleaved draws, cap $3.40 (D439 at most about $39.83).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8742:**The run** ($1.31; D439 about $37.74): A2 wrote H20 2 of 2 and memory 2 of 2 where the frozen arm declined 2 of 2. Both arms declined\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8781:No further spend on this route. D439 is at about $37.74 of $40.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8801:D439 is at about $37.74 of $40.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8820:- **The price, stated plainly:** about $4.90 to $6.60 before retries, a cap of at least about $9, beyond D439's remaining $2.26.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8831:- **Authority:** D426's \"no fifth Stage A is sent\" is Alex's specific decision and \"remains in force\". D439's later general delegation\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8842:- D439 is at about $37.74 of $40.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8875:    - Caps: luna $0.10 and Opus $2.15, within D439's remaining $2.26.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8912:- **Spending:** D439 stands at about $39.29 of $40, including run-1's $0.026.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9116:## D655 · 2026-11-17 · Council consensus (D439, D654): send the paired test of the narrow passage v5.5 on astra, shared cap $3.60\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9189:- **Decided** (D439; Alex active, informed):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9287:- **Decided (D439; reversible):**\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9318:- **Decided (consensus; D439's limits):**\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9446:- **Read as:** his word to run D665's comparison once its run plan passes a council review. As D563 and D439 read \"his word\", this covers that one\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9460:## D667 · 2026-11-17 · Under D666 and D439 (council, run-plan rounds 1–10): the release comparison's run plan and the rules it takes for this run\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9494:     reviewers read \"same day\" differently, so the council took the cheaper, reversible course (D439).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9581:- **Split, the cheaper and safer course taken (D439):**\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10042:## D677 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison's goal loop is closed; the old system stays; no paid work continues (council consensus, D439/D544)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10050:  - A verdict needs a full comparison, about $110, above D439's $40 ceiling.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10097:- **Ceiling:** $5 on a new ledger. The estimate is about $1.4 for c8 and about $0.2 for judging. This is within D439's $40.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10172:  - a new $2 ledger for the separating test, inside D439's $40.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10205:    Claude, every round logged. The limits of D439 stand: the frozen ruler and the frozen production files never change, nothing is\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10206:    pushed, deployed or committed unasked, credentials and caps are untouched, and paid spend stays inside D439's $40;\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10351:- **Spend, an error of mine.** The last D439 tally was about $39.29 of $40 (D647). D679, D682 and D684 then said \"inside D439's $40\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10353:  - Under the two readings, D439 stands at about $39.65 (only `phase1b`, $0.36) or about $44.42 (the merge test's $2.13, `phase1` at\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11656:## D750 · 2026-11-23 · The D749 writer test is INCONCLUSIVE with no failed line; council 65 (under D439): one bullet-2 sentence on reaffirmed targets, then a second $0 writer test\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11659:  - D439 governs: the council decides reversibly, no paid send (its ceiling is spent), nothing committed.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11681:  is regis