{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#|§0'\"' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg --files --hidden | rg -i 'council.*72|72.*council|release.*(builder|check)' | head -80\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#|§0'\"' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg --files --hidden | rg -i 'council.*72|72.*council|release.*(builder|check)' | head -80\"","aggregated_output":"1:# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n12:## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n25:## 1. Goal (end to end)\n31:## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n57:## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n67:| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n70:## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n93:## 5. What to do\n120:## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n168:## 7. Process (no drift)\n179:## 8. Steps and where we are\n193:## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/council-codex-72.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/council-codex-72.jsonl\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/council-codex-72.stderr\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
