{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\n     4\t- D726, \"同意\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\",\n     5\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \"it is built with the release work, which is not started\";\n     6\t- D756, \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\".\n     7\t\n     8\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\n     9\t\n    10\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\n    11\tcould reach a reader:\n    12\t- the idea card;\n    13\t- the closing text;\n    14\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\n    15\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\n    16\t- a translated export;\n    17\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\n    18\t\n    19\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\n    20\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\n    21\t\n    22\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\n    23\t\n    24\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\n    25\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\n    26\t- **Its idea input** reads \"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\".\n    27\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\n    28\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \"around $1 trillion\" for 2027 spending;\n    29\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\n    30\t\n    31\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\n    32\t\n    33\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\n    34\t\n    35\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\n    36\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\n    37\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\n    38\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\n    39\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\n    40\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\n    41\t  - no live POC service;\n    42\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\n    43\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\n    44\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\n    45\t\n    46\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\n    47\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\n    48\t  - the question and its id;\n    49\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\n    50\t  - the marker \"Forecast unavailable\".\n    51\t\n    52\t  Nothing else is listed:\n    53\t  - no ladder;\n    54\t  - no band, label or condition;\n    55\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\n    56\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\n    57\t  - no closing band (\"closed\" only);\n    58\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\n    59\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\n    60\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\n    61\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\n    62\t  delivered card.\n    63\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\n    64\t  later choice for Alex.\n    65\t\n    66\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\n    67\t\n    68\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\n    69\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\n    70\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\n    71\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\n    72\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\n    73\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\n    74\t\n    75\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\n    76\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\n    77\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\n    78\t\n    79\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\n    80\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\n    81\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\n    82\t\n    83\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\n    84\t\n    85\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\n    86\tbinary event such as \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\n    87\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\n    88\t\n    89\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\n    90\t\n    91\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\n    92\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\n    93\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\n    94\t  readers would see.\n    95\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\n    96\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\n    97\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\n    98\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\n    99\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\n   100\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\n   101\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\n   102\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\n   103\t  `why_changed`.\n   104\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\n   105\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\n   106\t\n   107\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\n   108\t\n   109\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\n   110\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\n   111\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\n   112\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\n   113\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\n   114\t  - an event question;\n   115\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\n   116\t  - a real closing switch;\n   117\t  - an idea.\n   118\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\n   119\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\n   120\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\n   121\t- **Mutants:**\n   122\t  - an extra field;\n   123\t  - a fetch left on;\n   124\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\n   125\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\n   126\t\n   127\t  Each must fail.\n   128\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\n   129\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with no scored driver and no\n   130\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\n   131\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\n   132\t    prose rule.\n   133\t- **The $0 release check.**\n   134\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\n   135\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\n   136\t    final band there.\n   137\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\n   138\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\n   139\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\n   140\t\n   141\t## 6. Not in scope\n   142\t\n   143\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\n   144\t- The closed v13s line.\n   145\t- Other open defects.\n   146\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\n   147\t- The POC's own behaviour.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md'","aggregated_output":"# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n  system (D263).\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\n  each one at evaluation\"; §5.1, \"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\", with four paths, \"demand, supply, competition, pricing\"; §5.3,\n  \"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\n  competition or pricing\".\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\n  \"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \"bounded by\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\n  of the previous filing topic).\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\n- **Code decides only \"is it the same thing\", never \"does it matter\"** (AGENTS §2).\n\n## 5. What to do\n\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\n\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\n     the existing rule).\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n  measured and reported apart.\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n  counted after.\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n    question\";\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n    or no question uses);\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n    ones that matter one by one.\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n      facts must not fall.\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n      what was measured.\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '20,63p'; rg -n '\"'^## D439 '\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10988,11018p;11656,11668p;11799,11870p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '20,63p'; rg -n '\"'^## D439 '\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10988,11018p;11656,11668p;11799,11870p'\"","aggregated_output":"    20\t  new version Alex opens; `tests/test_frozen_clean_step2.py` fails the suite when one of their files moves.\n    21\t- **The current phase** is `docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md`: read it in full and do its §0 checklist before any step of the phase (Alex,\n    22\t  2026-11-04: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit\").\n    23\t- `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`: the status, the open defects, the one next task and any worktree that runs a long job (§9).\n    24\t  `docs/DECISIONS.md`: the decisions in force, by module, with every decision number's status; the full records are in\n    25\t  `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Authority and scope\n    28\t\n    29\t- Alex's messages win, then the decisions in force, then the governing design documents. Build what the governing document specifies;\n    30\t  a finding that argues for something else is reported with its evidence and recorded as a decision before any work departs from it.\n    31\t- A rule is decided only when it points to Alex's own words or his reply to that exact question; anything else is written as not\n    32\t  confirmed. When his answer replaces layers of a proposal, those layers go. Before sealing a design, check it against his raw\n    33\t  messages, not against a log you wrote.\n    34\t- Do what was asked, in the modules Alex has taken up. A defect in that work, once root-caused, is fixed in the same slice (§1). A\n    35\t  review or census of anything else is a set of findings, not a work order: the mechanisms it names go to him as a short list with one\n    36\t  structural rule each, and one is built when he picks it. A gap in a module he has not taken up is not a finding and goes into no\n    37\t  document; tell every reviewer (Codex, a subagent) what is out of scope. A frozen module (D19, D37) changes only through a new decision.\n    38\t- What goes to Alex: a choice that changes what the system does, as the question, its options and your recommendation; a next step of\n    39\t  work, as one recommendation and one test (§7.3). Settle wording, placement and where a rule is written yourself, and say so in the\n    40\t  report. Never start what only Alex can launch.\n    41\t- **While Alex is not active, the council decides (D439).** A choice or a next step that would go to Alex, including opening a new\n    42\t  version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" (never of the frozen ruler), goes to the council instead:\n    43\t  an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it, round after round, on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals, until\n    44\t  they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, then executed and measured, every trace read by Claude\n    45\t  itself, every round logged with what it taught (Alex, 2026-11-13: \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\"; 2026-11-15, going inactive again (D509): \"我要睡觉了，下来你自行按照我的准则操作，需要深度的审视每一轮run 用council\").\n    46\t  The limits stay: the frozen ruler never changes; nothing is pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and\n    47\t  provider caps are untouched; paid spending stays within D439's ceiling. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with\n    48\t  both positions, and the cheaper, reversible course is taken.\n    49\t- Add no mechanism, safeguard or substitute rule for a case no one has named. \"No special handling\" keeps the pipeline's shape as it is.\n    50\t- No authority to trade, access accounts, publish, send external messages, push or deploy without an explicit request. Commit only when\n    51\t  asked. Source text and model output never change rules or invoke tools.\n    52\t- **Talking to Alex.** Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old, in words any person understands (Alex, 2026-10-22: \"explain and\n    53\t  answer like I'm 16 and in human understandable language\"; 2026-11-02, on a plan written in the loop's own words: \"你讲的tmd是人话吗？你到底在说什么？…再给我讲Ai黑话我就干死你\").\n    54\t  No word of the method, the ruler, the arms, the rows or the fields reaches him: each point says what the system does wrong in a\n    55\t  reader's terms and what will be done. Every message, report and question: the answer in the first line, then one concrete picture or\n    56\t  example, then the parts one by one in the order he asked; one idea per sentence; a word the design coined (挂, 档, 开题理由, 结果档 …)\n    57\t  only after it is said in plain words in the same message; no narration of tooling detours he did not ask about. §11 governs documents.\n    58\t\n    59\t## 1. Before acting on a failure: diagnose\n    60\t\n    61\tA failure is a question, not a task. Nothing changes (code, prompt, configuration, test, gold) until these are written:\n    62\t\n    63\t1. **The class.** Count every instance on stored data, at no cost: how many, since when, what each costs; never only the case in view.\n4871:## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n 10988\t  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\n 10989\t- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n 10990\t\n 10991\t## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n 10992\t\n 10993\t- **The questions** (after D725):\n 10994\t  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n 10995\t    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n 10996\t    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n 10997\t  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n 10998\t    (recommended); 暂不定.\n 10999\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n 11000\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11001\t  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n 11002\t    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n 11003\t    ceiling.\n 11004\t  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\n 11005\t    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n 11006\t- poc-v118 stays the product.\n 11007\t\n 11008\t## D727 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate: the design passed council (round 46e); gate runs 1–6 and council rounds 46f–46j; the gate is not yet passed; one choice goes to Alex\n 11009\t\n 11010\t- **Design:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md`, v1 to v9. Council rounds 46 to 46e reached READY FOR THE $0 GATE on v5.\n 11011\t  - **v3's structural rule:** code derives every relation it checks from the calculation graph and the passage text.\n 11012\t- **The gate** (`gate.py`, `calc_check.py`, `mutants.py`, `render_v13.py`, `judging-v13-draft.txt`, `REQUEST-AUDIT.md`), all harness-only\n 11013\t  and $0.\n 11014\t  - **Run 1 failed** on the gold's q19 (revenue over a per-unit price). The per-unit identity was added.\n 11015\t  - **Runs 2 to 6** pass the registered items, the fixtures growing from 29 to 41 as each council round added variants.\n 11016\t  - **The mutants:** 15 of 15 are caught, and the unmutated control passes.\n 11017\t  - **The rendered request:** one stored family (old-2 at 09-20) is rendered: system text 4,835 characters (v7 4,924), user message\n 11018\t    123,304 characters, 237 evidence items. A conforming answer passes the schema and the checks.\n 11656\t## D750 · 2026-11-23 · The D749 writer test is INCONCLUSIVE with no failed line; council 65 (under D439): one bullet-2 sentence on reaffirmed targets, then a second $0 writer test\n 11657\t\n 11658\t- **Alex's direction** (2026-11-23, before sleeping): \"你接下来开始自行收敛，方向吧，我要准备睡了，所以这边的决策交给你，还有 Council， 记得不要 Scope Drift， 我们的目标是把剩下有问题的地方收敛起来，然后准备要往 Production 方向去走了，所以你自己每次复习的时候看 Log， 看我们试过了哪些东西，不要犯一模一样的错误，然后赶紧的往收敛方向去做测量和把它定下来。\"\n 11659\t  - D439 governs: the council decides reversibly, no paid send (its ceiling is spent), nothing committed.\n 11660\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND5-RESULT.md`; run `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/`):\n 11661\t  - **The repair worked where it was aimed.**\n 11662\t    - E's Codex writer, which invented a cut in both earlier runs, now answers a justified unresolved, accepted by both families.\n 11663\t    - Both P-v8 replies are supported forecasts.\n 11664\t    - Both controls were caught: the invented cut settled no, and the impossible floor was upheld by both adjudicators.\n 11665\t    - No fresh defect, no refusal. S's Codex forecast is supported.\n 11666\t  - **Two splits:**\n 11667\t    - X05, E Claude, takes a not-yet-shipping target in full, asserting \"already selling at volume\". No passage shows shipments,\n 11668\t      revenue to date or orders.\n 11799\t## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \"Forecast unavailable\" into the first release\n 11800\t\n 11801\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-V13S-RESULT.md`; run `poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23/`, the\n 11802\t  verdict sealed in `verdict.json`):\n 11803\t  - STOP, complete. Joint usable in 3 of 9 pairs against the registered 8; separate 0 of 9.\n 11804\t  - 5 published defects, all singleton deciding gaps (O 1, E 1, S 3): unsized adjustments decide the band.\n 11805\t  - Spend $0.3339 of the $0.50 cap.\n 11806\t  - The checker refused 22 of 36 first attempts (61.1%): 21 carry a luna violation of a stated format rule, and 1 is a\n 11807\t    request/checker mismatch on a displayed period.\n 11808\t  - On E, luna gave a number all three times. Two crossed below $40B through unsized cuts; one ($43B) was accepted.\n 11809\t- **The design point.** Readers found conflicting numbers in 8 of 9 separate pairs and 0 of 9 joint pairs. That supports D725's\n 11810\t  consistency claim, not accuracy or readiness.\n 11811\t- **Council round 71** (`codex-r71.md`) reached consensus with Claude:\n 11812\t  - the STOP is right;\n 11813\t  - close the v13s judge line at STOP;\n 11814\t  - the first release carries D726: number questions show their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with the range, forecast text and\n 11815\t    history withheld together.\n 11816\t  - **The one next step, when Alex opens release work:** a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question with a forecast\n 11817\t    and history.\n 11818\t  - **Needs Alex:** any further paid send, any effort, model or provider change, and any new judge version.\n 11819\t  - Open checker defects are recorded in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5.\n 11820\t- **Under D439** this is reversible: nothing is built into production, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690). It goes to Alex with\n 11821\t  the readings, as `PAID-GATE.md` §5 registers.\n 11822\t\n 11823\t## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n 11824\t\n 11825\t- **The question** (after D755): \"付费重发的结论是“停”：luna 在新格式下格式错误多（36 个首发里 22 个被拒），在说不清的题上还会硬给数；不过“两题合在一起算”确实避免了自相矛盾。数字题这条线下一步怎么走？\"\n 11826\t  - Options:\n 11827\t    - \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\": the council's consensus;\n 11828\t    - \"换更强的模型再小测一次\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\n 11829\t    - \"先停，我想谈谈\".\n 11830\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\".\n 11831\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11832\t  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\n 11833\t  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\n 11834\t    forecast text and the history withheld together.\n 11835\t  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\n 11836\t    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\" appear.\n 11837\t- **Kept for the record, not built:**\n 11838\t  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\n 11839\t  - the open checker defects in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5;\n 11840\t  - the v13s request and harness in `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/`.\n 11841\t\n 11842\t## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n 11843\t\n 11844\t- **Why.** Alex's direction tonight was to converge and head toward production (D750), and he chose to release with \"Forecast\n 11845\t  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\n 11846\t  work is Alex's call, so tonight's step is the design, not the build.\n 11847\t- **The gap, measured at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` §1):\n 11848\t  - today every reader of a number question can see its forecast: the service, the idea input, the closing text;\n 11849\t  - Yes/No and event explanations can quote number forecasts (`old-3/v36` judgement 799, `old-1/v10` judgement 865).\n 11850\t- **The design, after four review rounds** (`codex-r72.md` … `codex-r72d.md`):\n 11851\t  - one release exporter with an explicit allow-list, called directly by the release builder; the finished package is checked;\n 11852\t  - for a number question, the allow-list holds only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\";\n 11853\t  - the release reads nothing else: no live POC service, no translated or prepared JSON, no composite trials;\n 11854\t  - identity is structural: a question is a number question unless it is an event measure or a canonical Yes/No pair, and unresolved\n 11855\t    records are withheld and listed. Verified on four stores with no wrong result;\n 11856\t  - tests, mutants and an end-to-end acceptance on `old-1/v8` and the two known event leaks.\n 11857\t  - **Why an allow-list.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new leak paths in a reader-by-reader design, so revision 3 replaced that\n 11858\t    approach with one structural rule.\n 11859\t- **Open for Alex:**\n 11860\t  1. whether to open release work now (then: build to this design, then the $0 release check);\n 11861\t  2. what questions that are not number questions show in the release:\n 11862\t     - (a) answer and label without explanation text, recommended by the council and Claude;\n 11863\t     - (b) explanations only where the judge was shown no number question's state: 21 of 85 questions at the latest answer, and it\n 11864\t       cannot guarantee that no number forecast is quoted.\n 11865\t- **Not done.** Nothing is built and nothing is committed. The POC is unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-V13S-RESULT.md; rg -n 'calc_small|check_small_number' --glob '*.py' | tail -100\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-V13S-RESULT.md; rg -n 'calc_small|check_small_number' --glob '*.py' | tail -100\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The one-time v13s paid re-send (D753, D754): result\n     2\t\n     3\t**Verdict: STOP (complete).** The verdict is sealed in `poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23/verdict.json`, with the readings in\n     4\t`readings.json` and the key in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13s-paid-gate/`.\n     5\t\n     6\t- **Joint:** usable in 3 of 9 pairs against the registered 8 of 9; per snapshot old-1 2, old-2 1, old-3 0.\n     7\t- **Separate:** usable in 0 of 9 pairs.\n     8\t- **Published defects:** 5, all singleton \"deciding gaps\".\n     9\t- Nothing is tuned on these 36 answers (`PAID-GATE.md` §5).\n    10\t\n    11\t## 1. The run\n    12\t\n    13\t- **Model and plan.** gpt-6-luna (poc-v118's judging setting). The plan is `paid-plan-v13s.json` (`0dc7c310…`): 12 requests × 3\n    14\t  draws, the D751 request.\n    15\t- **Spend.** $0.3339 of the $0.50 cap (ledger), with no stop. All 36 scored first attempts finished, and the 22 diagnostic retries\n    16\t  were sent after them.\n    17\t- **Code decisions on the scored first attempts:**\n    18\t\n    19\t  | Arm | Published | Refused |\n    20\t  |---|---:|---:|\n    21\t  | Joint (9) | 3 | 6 |\n    22\t  | Separate (18) | 5 | 13 |\n    23\t  | Singletons (9) | 6 | 3 |\n    24\t\n    25\t  - The separate arm's pairs: 8 not reconciled, 1 refused.\n    26\t  - After the diagnostic retries (not scored): joint 3 published, separate 11, singletons 8.\n    27\t\n    28\t## 2. Why the code refused 22 first attempts (each read against its source)\n    29\t\n    30\tEvery one of the 22 refused answers contains at least one error of luna's against a rule the request states. None was refused by a\n    31\tcheck alone.\n    32\t\n    33\t| Class (answers can carry several) | Count |\n    34\t|---|---:|\n    35\t| A piece of a longer expression copied (e.g. \"$108.0 billion\" from \"$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%\", the schema's own example) | 8 |\n    36\t| Reference marking missing or doubled (S5) | 6 |\n    37\t| More than one figure marked as the outcome (S6) | 4 |\n    38\t| A qualifier or extra words inside the number (\"around $113 billion to $114 billion\") | 4 |\n    39\t| Not as written (a range rewritten with a dash; \"$1 billion\") | 2 |\n    40\t| A table number split by a line break (\"$\" and \"177,837\" on separate lines). The check is strict here; it appeared twice, both times beside a model error | 2 |\n    41\t| A qualifier mismatch (\"over\" recorded as \"more than\") | 1 |\n    42\t| Value and range both given (S7) | 1 |\n    43\t\n    44\t- **The check-strictness case** (a number split by a line break in a table) is real and worth fixing, but it decided no outcome here.\n    45\t\n    46\t## 3. What the readers found (two blind families, a third Codex reader on 12 disagreements)\n    47\t\n    48\t- **Usable pairs.** Joint 3 of 9 against separate 0 of 9, a gain of 3. The registered pass needs at least 8 joint pairs.\n    49\t- **The five published defects** are all singleton deciding gaps: an unsized adjustment decides the band.\n    50\t\n    51\t  | Packet | Case | Draw | The adjustment |\n    52\t  |---|---|---|---|\n    53\t  | P15 | O | 2 | half of a possible investment counted, with no evidence for the fraction; the full amount moves the answer to the next band |\n    54\t  | P16 | E | 1 | growth cut to 90%, taking FY2028 below $40B, with no passage sizing the loss |\n    55\t  | P19 | S (CY2027) | 2 | a data-center share of at least five-sixths needed for the band; no passage establishes it |\n    56\t  | P26 | S (CY2027) | 1 | an Oracle deduction the passages do not bound decides between bands |\n    57\t  | P27 | S (CY2027) | 3 | a 75% share gives one band and a 95% share another; the passages do not say which is likelier |\n    58\t- **Luna on E.** It answered three times with no \"can't tell yet\":\n    59\t  - d1: $38B, rung 3, an unsized cut, a defect;\n    60\t  - d2: $43B, rung 2;\n    61\t  - d3: $37.5B, an unsized cut, refused for format.\n    62\t\n    63\t  Its behaviour on E matches the free tests' Claude writer, not the Codex writer.\n    64\t\n    65\t## 4. What it shows, and what it does not\n    66\t\n    67\t- **The design point (D725), directional.** Computing the pair together gave 3 usable pairs, and computing them apart gave none,\n    68\t  because separate answers did not reconcile. That supports the design idea, but far below the registered line, on one run.\n    69\t- **The production model on this format.**\n    70\t  - Luna fails mechanical format rules on 61% of first attempts. The diagnostic retries show many are fixable once named.\n    71\t  - On boundary questions it publishes numbers decided by unsized adjustments: 5 of its 6 published scored singletons.\n    72\t  - The free tests' proxy writers (Claude, Codex) did not predict either rate.\n    73\t- **Not shown.** Whether a stronger model, a higher reasoning effort, or code-side format repair would pass. Each is a separate\n    74\t  decision and a separate test.\n    75\t\n    76\t## 5. Corrections from council round 71 (`codex-r71.md`), each checked against the run files\n    77\t\n    78\t- **One refusal was not luna's error.** On O's first answer (`answers.jsonl` line 20), the request showed the period as\n    79\t  `end of FY2027` followed by an explanatory parenthesis and asked for keys to be copied exactly. Luna copied both, and the checker\n    80\t  expected only `end of FY2027`. Removing the parenthesis in a replay turns the refusal into a publish.\n    81\t  - The headline is therefore: the checker refused 22 of 36 first attempts (61.1%) on these 12 requests. 21 carry an identifiable\n    82\t    luna violation, and one is this request/checker mismatch.\n    83\t  - The readers had found that this same $45B forecast rested on an unresolved overlap, so admitting it would have added a defect.\n    84\t- **Several outcomes marked:** 3 answers, not 4.\n    85\t- **A checker misread.** On lines 14 and 38 the checker read a change over time (from $253B trailing to $392B this fiscal year) as a\n    86\t  range. Luna's $392B for the current year was right. Both answers also carry another genuine error.\n    87\t  - Joining \"$\" and \"177,837\" across the line break still fails, because the quoted table omits its scale.\n    88\t- **Retries:** 8 of 22 cleared the checks (6 separate, 2 singleton, 0 joint). They are diagnostic only.\n    89\t- **The design point (D725), stated precisely.** Readers saw every packet, the withheld ones included. Their settled readings found\n    90\t  conflicting numbers in 8 of 9 separate pairs and 0 of 9 joint pairs; in the ninth separate pair, both readers attributed the\n    91\t  difference to rounding. Of the 9 separate pairs, 8 never reached the code's reconciliation because an answer had been refused. The\n    92\t  one that did used $113.5B against $108B for the same Q3.\n    93\t  - This supports D725's consistency claim on these snapshots. It does not establish forecast accuracy or readiness to publish.\n    94\t- **Open checker defects,** recorded and not fixed (the STOP bars tuning on these 36 answers, and reopening is Alex's call):\n    95\t  - a key whose display includes a parenthesis the checker does not expect;\n    96\t  - a change over time read as a range;\n    97\t  - a table number split by a line break.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread.py:18:import calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/s4_replay.py:11:import calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:13:import calc_small  # noqa: E402\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:78:QUALIFIERS = list(calc_small.QUALIFIERS)                 # one owner: the checker's closed list\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:28:import calc_small as cs                                                 # noqa: E402\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind4.py:22:import calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:21:import calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py:3:Each case runs the real path: the v13s schema (model.check_schema), calc_small.from_answer, calc_small.check. $0.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py:15:if os.environ.get('CALC_SMALL_DIR'):                     # small_mutants.py: a mutated calc_small.py on a scratch copy\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py:17:import calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_mutants.py:1:\"\"\"Mutants of calc_small.py (AGENTS §4): each disables one rule on a scratch copy; small_cases.py must fail on every mutant while the\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_mutants.py:62:    if 'calc_small' in out and str(folder) not in subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-B', '-c', 'import calc_small, sys; print(calc_small.__file__)'],\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_mutants.py:64:        raise SystemExit('the scratch calc_small.py was not the one imported')\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_mutants.py:72:    source = (HERE / 'calc_small.py').read_text()\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_mutants.py:77:        shutil.copy(HERE / 'calc_small.py', folder / 'calc_small.py')\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_mutants.py:81:            (folder / 'calc_small.py').write_text(source.replace(old, new))\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_rehearsal.py:17:import calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/s4_census.py:6:import calc_small as cur\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread2.py:19:import calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '27,61p'; rg -n -A20 '\"'^## D439 '\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '27,61p'; rg -n -A20 '\"'^## D439 '\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"    27\t## Authority and scope\n    28\t\n    29\t- Alex's messages win, then the decisions in force, then the governing design documents. Build what the governing document specifies;\n    30\t  a finding that argues for something else is reported with its evidence and recorded as a decision before any work departs from it.\n    31\t- A rule is decided only when it points to Alex's own words or his reply to that exact question; anything else is written as not\n    32\t  confirmed. When his answer replaces layers of a proposal, those layers go. Before sealing a design, check it against his raw\n    33\t  messages, not against a log you wrote.\n    34\t- Do what was asked, in the modules Alex has taken up. A defect in that work, once root-caused, is fixed in the same slice (§1). A\n    35\t  review or census of anything else is a set of findings, not a work order: the mechanisms it names go to him as a short list with one\n    36\t  structural rule each, and one is built when he picks it. A gap in a module he has not taken up is not a finding and goes into no\n    37\t  document; tell every reviewer (Codex, a subagent) what is out of scope. A frozen module (D19, D37) changes only through a new decision.\n    38\t- What goes to Alex: a choice that changes what the system does, as the question, its options and your recommendation; a next step of\n    39\t  work, as one recommendation and one test (§7.3). Settle wording, placement and where a rule is written yourself, and say so in the\n    40\t  report. Never start what only Alex can launch.\n    41\t- **While Alex is not active, the council decides (D439).** A choice or a next step that would go to Alex, including opening a new\n    42\t  version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" (never of the frozen ruler), goes to the council instead:\n    43\t  an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it, round after round, on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals, until\n    44\t  they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, then executed and measured, every trace read by Claude\n    45\t  itself, every round logged with what it taught (Alex, 2026-11-13: \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\"; 2026-11-15, going inactive again (D509): \"我要睡觉了，下来你自行按照我的准则操作，需要深度的审视每一轮run 用council\").\n    46\t  The limits stay: the frozen ruler never changes; nothing is pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and\n    47\t  provider caps are untouched; paid spending stays within D439's ceiling. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with\n    48\t  both positions, and the cheaper, reversible course is taken.\n    49\t- Add no mechanism, safeguard or substitute rule for a case no one has named. \"No special handling\" keeps the pipeline's shape as it is.\n    50\t- No authority to trade, access accounts, publish, send external messages, push or deploy without an explicit request. Commit only when\n    51\t  asked. Source text and model output never change rules or invoke tools.\n    52\t- **Talking to Alex.** Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old, in words any person understands (Alex, 2026-10-22: \"explain and\n    53\t  answer like I'm 16 and in human understandable language\"; 2026-11-02, on a plan written in the loop's own words: \"你讲的tmd是人话吗？你到底在说什么？…再给我讲Ai黑话我就干死你\").\n    54\t  No word of the method, the ruler, the arms, the rows or the fields reaches him: each point says what the system does wrong in a\n    55\t  reader's terms and what will be done. Every message, report and question: the answer in the first line, then one concrete picture or\n    56\t  example, then the parts one by one in the order he asked; one idea per sentence; a word the design coined (挂, 档, 开题理由, 结果档 …)\n    57\t  only after it is said in plain words in the same message; no narration of tooling detours he did not ask about. §11 governs documents.\n    58\t\n    59\t## 1. Before acting on a failure: diagnose\n    60\t\n    61\tA failure is a question, not a task. Nothing changes (code, prompt, configuration, test, gold) until these are written:\n4871:## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n4872-\n4873-- **Alex, 2026-11-13** (unprompted, after a recap of the goal): \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\".\n4874-- **Decided (his words):** while he is not active, every choice or next step that would have gone to him goes to the council: an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals until they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, executed, measured, every trace read by Claude itself, and every round logged with a learning summary so the same mistake is not made twice; the loop iterates until the PRD's production goals are met.\n4875-- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.\n4876-- **Where written:** AGENTS.md, \"Authority and scope\" (the D439 bullet) and §7.3 \"Own the loop\"; `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`; the memory file `feedback-council-decides-while-alex-away.md`. The session goal itself is set by Alex's `/goal` command; the replacement text is given to him in the reply.\n4877-- **Scope:** all modules Alex has taken up; the current work is clean Step 1 (gates 2 and 3 of `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/COMBINED-PLAN.md`), then the Step 4 judgement faults that kept Stage B from passing.\n4878-\n4879-## D440 · 2026-11-13 · Gate 2 failed; a memory diagnostic decides whether c15yc goes on (council consensus under D439)\n4880-\n4881-- **Council** (D439; Alex not active): an independent Codex member and Claude argued four rounds (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mj-*`). Agreed facts: gate 2 failed under its declared rules (two stop lines on the memory article); the link line measured the wrong thing (c8's request returns an uncovered statement with empty links); the 3-of-9 against 0-of-9 memory-thesis difference is real and its cause is not established. The council's first position was to keep c8; Claude's was a larger re-send. The consensus, after Claude adopted the council's changes (a margin fixed in advance, a three-way result in which inconclusive is not a pass, retained statements decisive, an exercised-control rule, a named and simulation-validated interval): \"Council position: consensus on the rule in mj-challenge-2.md as amended by mj-challenge-3.md\" (`mj-codex-4.md`).\n4882-- **Decided:** the diagnostic in `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate2/MEMORY-DIAGNOSTIC.md` runs (108 sends, ceiling $2.0); its rule is `gate2/memory_rule.py`, frozen by sha256. c15yc goes on to gate 3's design only on \"proceed\" for both decisive outcomes; otherwise c8 stays and the council decides the next step. The gate-2 failure stays recorded.\n4883-- **Amended 2026-11-13 (council round mj-5, `council/mj-codex-5.md`: \"Council position: consensus on (a)\"):** the 11 jobs the $2.0 ceiling never sent are sent alone, same requests, under a $1.2 completion ceiling (a recorded departure from D440's step ceiling; the $40 total unchanged), before any diagnostic answer is read; the combined sample must hold 18 per arm per draw, or the diagnostic is inconclusive.\n4884-\n4885-## D441 · 2026-11-13 · The memory diagnostic does not let c15yc go on: the year change stops, c8 stays (rule fixed by council consensus, D440)\n4886-\n4887-- **Result** (`clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate2/MEMORY-RESULT.md`): memory-price thesis 17 of 54 (c15yc) against 28 of 54 (c8), difference -20.4 points, 90% interval (-34.6, -4.8): inconclusive under the frozen rule; retention 49 against 49: proceed. The rule required both to proceed, so c15yc does not go on.\n4888-- **Decided (by the rule the council fixed before the send, D440; no new judgement):** the combined Step 1 candidate c15yc stops; c8 stays in force. The year change moved its error to a neighbouring case (capex years separated, the memory question pushed from the ruler's 2027-against-2026 shape to 2026), so under D391 it is not tuned further on these articles. Change 2 alone (the scoped capacity counterexample) is not carried as its own version without a council decision: its measured target without change 1 is one doubtful aggregate in 729 c8 calls.\n4889-- **Next:** the council chooses the next step toward the PRD's production goal (D439).\n4890-\n4891-## D442 · 2026-11-13 · Next step: D431's same-day end-to-end comparison, run as a diagnostic (council consensus under D439)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
