{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72d.md | head -80; rg -n -i 'release work|release engineering|open.*release|start.*release' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -45\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t1. Revision 4 adds the package boundary and acceptance case that 72c requested. The builder must call the exporter directly, and the check covers the finished package. The `old-1/v8` idea card must show its sources and “Forecast unavailable,” with no scored driver or substitute band. The same package must preserve both event labels and omit their spending forecasts. I found no unrelated change. [Revision 3 snapshot:15](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:15) · [Design:37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:37) · [Design:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:129)\n     2\t2. One prose rule now covers events and Yes/No questions, including all 85 overlapping cases. The figures match 72c. Option (b) would preserve explanations for 21 of 85 latest answers and 73 of 73 historical answers in the sealed ledger. The design recommends (a) to Alex. Under (a), I found no remaining route in the design for a stored number forecast to reach a release reader. [72c:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md:5) · [Design:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Design:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:98)\n     3\t3. **One correction from 72c is incomplete.** Line 97 still tells Alex that an explanation kept under (b) “cannot quote a number forecast.” Line 102 correctly says it can. A Yes/No answer can repeat a spending forecast from its previous explanation even when the current request shows no number question directly. Delete the sentence spanning lines 96–97 that makes the guarantee. [Design:96](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:96) · [Design:102](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:102) · [judging.py:211](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:211)\n     4\t\n     5\t**Verdict — not ready as written.** The contradictory guarantee is the only blocker. Once removed, the design is ready to hand to release work when Alex opens it, with §4’s choice still his and **(a) recommended**.562:- Changed by D32: the open item is settled (one release per item; no separate XBRL; no price-specific rule).\n2515:- Probe ([role_probe.py](research/2026-10-26-thesis-admission-v12/role_probe.py), `poc/reports/2026-10-26-admission-v12/role-probe/`): the gold's 20 items re-sent with the stored v12 request's user message and v13's system prompt and schema, three samples each, sifted and scored at the candidate level against the gold's must-open and must-not-open keys; the stored v12 answers of two runs (r3, r4) are the controls. Must-open keys proposed: v12 9/15 and 8/15, v13 26/45 (8.7 per sample); must-not-open keys proposed: v12 0 and 1, v13 11/174 (3.7 per sample: a tax-rate thesis from the press release in two samples, a Taiwan proceeding in two, a run-rate thesis); candidates 30, 30, 33 per sample. $0.09.\n2866:- No effect: two wordings of the standard's first test for opening a question (ruled-out 6 to 5 and 5; the excluded-kinds wording lost the obligation question on page 3); deleting the release-figures clause; tying kind (1) to the subject company.\n2940:- Decided: role-v42 replaces role-v29 as the extraction request; `scripts/replay.py` defaults to `poc/config/poc-v58.json`, which differs from `poc-v45` only in the ten extraction prompt versions (T*-v42). What it buys, pooled over the five runs on the development set: core kept 238.4 against 240.4 of 258 draw-hits (run differences −4, −10, −2, +4, +2), supporting kept in two draws 153.8 against 154.8 of 181, sentences the gold rejects kept 102.8 against 139.8 per draw, statements outside the gold 123.0 against 162.2 per draw; the test set shows the same pattern. What it costs: about 15 questions per full run that the gold says must not open, on release dates of small products, features and services (most from one article), against about 0 for role-v29 (`loop-log.md` rows 15–18).\n4001:- Remove the separate coverage-start report reading tied to seeded questions and do not add an earnings report as background to each news extraction request. This supersedes D363–D366 to the extent they require that separate report import and seeded default. An earnings release or filing arriving as an actual input remains a normal item under D28; existing research questions remain extraction context. Historical seeds, gold, results and records remain historical, not a new active starting library.\n9435:  3. **Back to Alex,** before any release engineering resumes: a practical lead (with the split cards for his spot check), a practical loss at\n10274:## D688 · 2026-11-20 · Under D687 (council M): no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone; to Alex, keep old and pause the hybrid's release line\n10298:  - No opening test and no M20 account probe are sent for release.\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n11005:    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n11816:  - **The one next step, when Alex opens release work:** a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question with a forecast\n11835:  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\n11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n11845:  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\n11860:  1. whether to open release work now (then: build to this design, then the $0 release check);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
