{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '9424,9440p;10315,10354p'; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '448,471p'\"","aggregated_output":"  9424\t       what counts as the same question), the controls, the versions and the rule.\n  9425\t  2. **What changes, explicitly:**\n  9426\t     - D548's use of D400's six lines as a release gate is superseded. The lines are reported on every ladder run.\n  9427\t     - The parts code decides stay hard: figure ranges meet end to end; the favourable end is stable; the due day is consistent at D400's 90%.\n  9428\t     - D431's frozen-reference reading of 07-01 to 07-14 is still produced and printed beside the comparison, not deciding. D665 supersedes D431\n  9429\t       on that point only.\n  9430\t     - Step 2's three checks stay as D427 and D431 set them.\n  9431\t     - Gate 2's unsupported lines become the guardrails, and its control line waits (D658).\n  9432\t     - Gate 4 folds in.\n  9433\t     - Gate 5 waits for a practical lead and Alex's word.\n  9434\t     - The absolute floors stay proposals, reported beside.\n  9435\t  3. **Back to Alex,** before any release engineering resumes: a practical lead (with the split cards for his spot check), a practical loss at\n  9436\t     once, no practical winner, too small or invalid, or no verdict by 2026-12-01.\n  9437\t- **Next:**\n  9438\t  - the comparison's design at $0: the exposure census, the frozen matter list and credit rules, the cards and controls, the replay plan and\n  9439\t    its spend guard;\n  9440\t  - council review;\n 10315\t  - no code or configuration changes.\n 10316\t- **Council N** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-*`): a fresh Codex thread (`01a1fac2…`, read-only, memories off) read the\n 10317\t  record cold, while Claude wrote its position apart. Both independently reached the same exit. Round 2 reached CONSENSUS, with three\n 10318\t  wording changes taken here.\n 10319\t- **Decided (council N, under D543):** the judge line and the c8 reading line close for now. Nothing is sent, and D198 is not changed.\n 10320\t  - **The judge.** The carried previous conclusion holds rejected forecasts in place.\n 10321\t    - On identical full evidence, 0 of 13 targets move with it, and 8 of 13 without it, with 0 of 8 controls moving.\n 10322\t    - Both blind readers support 4 net repairs, against the 5 required. The 4 are four test cases, M14 (four companies' 2027 capex)\n 10323\t      twice, in two of three old draws.\n 10324\t    - In the separate test with the usual limited evidence, the frozen gold reads 44.3 against v7's 45.0, with China share regressed.\n 10325\t    - Every remaining lever changes D198, and every big numeric bet on this corpus has been read by the design.\n 10326\t  - **c8** delivered the decisive statements but showed no improvement in the final answers tested. It adds about $24 to old's about\n 10327\t    $9 over 82 days.\n 10328\t- **Reopening conditions:**\n 10329\t  - **Judge.** Eight eligible failures on fresh questions.\n 10330\t    - \"Fresh\" means a question the design never read, counted once across draws, with close variants excluded (council I).\n 10331\t    - New evidence on a read question can show whether a repair holds over time. It does not count toward the eight.\n 10332\t    - Matched supported controls, and a source-checked summary of the omitted facts worth testing (D198 option 2), are also needed.\n 10333\t    - Then the D198 choice and its price go to Alex. A paid test needs his approval and funding.\n 10334\t    - Processing the 523 later articles (09-21..10-22) would cost about $2.5 a draw before readers, with no assurance of enough new\n 10335\t      questions.\n 10336\t  - **c8.** A traced case where:\n 10337\t    - old missed a decisive fact;\n 10338\t    - c8 delivers it;\n 10339\t    - the final answer it could change is named.\n 10340\t\n 10341\t    A paired test with the same judge and question would then show whether it helps.\n 10342\t  - **A future test's pass criteria** (proposed, not confirmed):\n 10343\t    - net repairs on distinct final forecasts, backed by both blind readers in 2 of 3 same-day pairs;\n 10344\t    - at least 4 at 8 targets;\n 10345\t    - no lost control and no added refusal;\n 10346\t    - frozen agreement at least v7's, with China share 3 of 3.\n 10347\t- **Not reopened:**\n 10348\t  - D368 item 2 (dependencies chosen at matching) stays open defect 4 in `CURRENT_STATE.md`, closed as a stretch by D542. None of the\n 10349\t    24 rejected answers traces to it.\n 10350\t  - The D260 stance-field order (D681) stays a recorded defect. J2a measured no effect from it.\n 10351\t- **Spend, an error of mine.** The last D439 tally was about $39.29 of $40 (D647). D679, D682 and D684 then said \"inside D439's $40\"\n 10352\t  with no tally.\n 10353\t  - Under the two readings, D439 stands at about $39.65 (only `phase1b`, $0.36) or about $44.42 (the merge test's $2.13, `phase1` at\n 10354\t    $2.64 by its ledger and `phase1b`).\n   448\t**The one next task: Alex chooses whether to open release work, and what non-number questions show (D757).** The \"Forecast\n   449\tunavailable\" release design is ready (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md`, council 72–72d).\n   450\t\n   451\t- **The design:**\n   452\t  - one allow-listed release exporter, called directly by the release builder; for a number question it emits only the question, its\n   453\t    sources and \"Forecast unavailable\";\n   454\t  - the release reads nothing else;\n   455\t  - number questions are identified by structure, and unresolved records are withheld.\n   456\t- **Choice 1 for Alex:** open release work now. Then: build to the design, then the $0 release check on `old-1/v8` and the two known\n   457\t  event leaks.\n   458\t- **Choice 2 for Alex:** what Yes/No and event questions show.\n   459\t  - (a) the answer and its label without explanation text, recommended;\n   460\t  - (b) explanations only where the judge saw no number question's state: 21 of 85 questions, with no guarantee against quoting.\n   461\t\n   462\tThe record of the D756 step:\n   463\t\n   464\t**Earlier next task (done, D757): when release work opens, a $0 check of the reader's screen for number questions (D756).** On a\n   465\tstored number question that has a forecast and history, the reader must see only the question, its sources and \"Forecast\n   466\tunavailable\".\n   467\t\n   468\t- **Alex closed the v13s judge line at its STOP** (D756: end the line, release with \"Forecast unavailable\"). Nothing from it enters the\n   469\t  product, and poc-v118 stays the product.\n   470\t- **No release work is open yet.** No other task is queued on the number-answer line.\n   471\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
