{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '190,230p'; rg -n 'fetch|library' poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js; nl -ba src/hivemind/idea_composite.py | sed -n '210,234p;251,258p;276,285p'; rg --files | rg '(build.*(ui|static|page)|mock_build).*\\\\.py\"'$'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"   190\t        for d in deps:\n   191\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   192\t            if not target:\n   193\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   194\t                continue\n   195\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   196\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   197\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   198\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   199\t            if full_dependencies:\n   200\t                lines.extend(_dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag))\n   201\t                continue\n   202\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   203\t    if themes:\n   204\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   205\t        for theme in themes:\n   206\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   207\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   208\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   209\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   210\t    if last:\n   211\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   212\t    else:\n   213\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   214\t    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n   215\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n   216\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n   217\t    return lines\n   218\t\n   219\t\n   220\tdef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   221\t    system, user, _ = request_parts(conn, view_id, prompt_version)\n   222\t    return system, user\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\tdef request_parts(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   226\t    \"\"\"(system text, user text, the ids the request lists), all from the same rows at the same ledger state: the evidence pieces it\n   227\t    prints, the dependencies it gives an entry (resolved ones; a dependency still waiting has no id to cite) and the themes it prints.\"\"\"\n   228\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n   229\t    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\n   230\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n23:const libraryRoot = document.getElementById('library');\n24:if (input && root && libraryRoot) {\n32:    const library = createLibrary(libraryRoot, { dataset: data });\n38:    const libraryRequest = new AbortController();\n47:    const libraryButton = document.getElementById('show-library');\n88:      libraryRoot.hidden = false;\n89:      libraryButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\n93:      library.close();\n94:      libraryRoot.hidden = true;\n96:      libraryButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');\n107:        app.showGraph({ day: library.getDay() });\n174:        day: library.getDay(),\n179:        day: library.getDay(),\n195:          asOf: library.getDay(),\n256:        const response = await fetch(`${API}/library`, { signal: libraryRequest.signal });\n259:        if (next.coverage !== 'library')\n260:          throw new Error('The service did not return a complete library');\n261:        if (libraryRequest.signal.aborted) return;\n262:        library.setDataset(next, { day: next.as_of }); // the supplied snapshot defines the displayed date (thesis-ui.md)\n270:    libraryButton.addEventListener('click', showLibrary);\n276:        libraryRequest.abort();\n277:        library.destroy();\n292:    libraryRoot.append(message);\n   210\t                               'raises_outcome_position': {'type': 'string', 'enum': list(positions)},\n   211\t                               'reason': {'type': 'string'},\n   212\t                               'weight_percent': {'type': 'integer', 'minimum': 1, 'maximum': 100},\n   213\t                               'weight_reason': {'type': 'string'}}}\n   214\t    choices = [item(t['view_id'], [str(rung['position']) for rung in t['ladder']]) for t in theses]\n   215\t    return {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,\n   216\t            'required': ['summary', 'outcome', 'claim_direction', 'composite'],\n   217\t            'properties': {'summary': {'type': 'string'}, 'outcome': {'type': 'string'},\n   218\t                           'claim_direction': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['higher', 'lower', 'unclear']},\n   219\t                           'composite': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'anyOf': choices} if choices else item()}}}\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\tdef bind_adoption(answer, selected, records, as_of, theses, schema):\n   223\t    \"\"\"Bind an answer checked against the exact schema that was sent; code checks only what a schema cannot say.\"\"\"\n   224\t    errors = model.check_schema(answer, schema)\n   225\t    if errors:\n   226\t        raise model.SchemaError('; '.join(errors))\n   227\t    if not answer['outcome'].strip():\n   228\t        raise model.SchemaError('composite: the assessed outcome must be named')\n   229\t    if answer['composite'] and answer['claim_direction'] == 'unclear':\n   230\t        raise model.SchemaError('composite: an unclear claim cannot have scored drivers')\n   231\t    first = {t['view_id']: str(t['ladder'][0]['position']) for t in theses}\n   232\t    allowed = {s['view_id'] for s in selected} & set(first)\n   233\t    drivers, seen, total = [], set(), 0\n   234\t    for entry in answer['composite']:\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\tdef contract(prompt_version, selected, ledger=None):\n   254\t    \"\"\"The schema, prose fields and binder belonging to each versioned composite prompt.\"\"\"\n   255\t    if prompt_version == 'idea-summary-v8':\n   256\t        theses = add_ladders(ledger, [{'view_id': entry['view_id']} for entry in selected], endpoints_only=True)\n   257\t        schema = adoption_schema(theses)\n   258\t        return schema, positive_prose, lambda answer, *args: bind_adoption(answer, *args, theses, schema)\n   276\t\n   277\tdef add_ladders(ledger, theses, endpoints_only=False):\n   278\t    \"\"\"Supply the immutable ordered outcomes, without copying evidence or guessing UI score orientation.\"\"\"\n   279\t    result = []\n   280\t    for thesis in theses:\n   281\t        rungs = store.rungs_of(ledger, thesis['view_id'])\n   282\t        if endpoints_only:\n   283\t            rungs = [rungs[0], rungs[-1]]\n   284\t        result.append({**thesis, 'ladder': [{key: rung[key] for key in ('position', 'label', 'condition')} for rung in rungs]})\n   285\t    return result\nscripts/mock_build.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A19 '\"'^## D690 '\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba scripts/mock_build.py | rg 'data\\\\.en|composite.trials|market|read_text|write_text' | tail -15; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72.md | tail -14\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A19 '\"'^## D690 '\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba scripts/mock_build.py | rg 'data\\\\.en|composite.trials|market|read_text|write_text' | tail -15; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72.md | tail -14\"","aggregated_output":"10360:## D690 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A: poc-v118 is the product, the research line rests until his new direction; the D681–D689 records are committed locally\n10361-\n10362-- **Alex's words** (2026-11-20), replying to the two items put to him after D689: \"1. OK 2. A\". Item 1 was a local commit of the\n10363-  D681–D689 records, not pushed. Item 2's options were:\n10364-  - **A**, recommended: poc-v118 is the product, and the research line rests until his new direction;\n10365-  - **B**, change the rules that bind the hybrid's lead: whether the library tracks other companies' own figures (5 matters, D688),\n10366-    and whether the judge carries its previous conclusion (D198). \"One bet, one question\" (D248) was not offered for change, because\n10367-    the comparison's list is finer than it;\n10368-  - **C**, new test questions from another company or a later NVIDIA window, at a price he would set.\n10369-- **Decided (Alex):** A. No improvement line on the hybrid, the judge, c8 or opening is open, and no paid send is open. The reopening\n10370-  conditions of D689 stand. B and C are not taken.\n10371-- **Done:** the D681–D690 records are committed on `clean-arch`, and nothing is pushed.\n10372-- **Asked next by Alex, in the same message:** a description of the end-to-end system (its components, how it runs, its current\n10373-  performance) and whether it is ready to go to production for testing. That answer is an assessment, recorded when it is given.\n10374-\n10375-## D691 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A after council Q: no daily wrapper yet; link related questions first, a $0 check then a few cents\n10376-\n10377-- **Alex's words** (2026-11-20): on the half-hour read of poc-v118's 09-20 output, \"dont' you take a look for me let the council tak\n10378-  ea crack at it\"; on the three options put to him after council Q, \"A\".\n10379-- **Council Q** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-q/RESULT.md`, consensus, $0): an analyst would use the\n    24\t    parser.add_argument('--composite-trials', type=Path, help='explicit JSON trial baskets for the Idea score preview')\n    25\t    parser.add_argument('--market-data', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/ui/data/nvda-2026-10-27.json', help='dated real stock-price snapshot for the Action preview')\n    28\t        data = json.loads(args.data.read_text())\n    54\t    market = subprocess.run(['node', str(ui / 'prepare-data.mjs'), '--market'], input=args.market_data.read_text(), capture_output=True, text=True)\n    55\t    if market.returncode:\n    56\t        print(market.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\n    57\t        market.check_returncode()\n    58\t    print(market.stderr.strip())\n    59\t    template = (ROOT / 'poc/mock/index.template.html').read_text()\n    62\t    page = page.replace('__MARKET_DATA__', market.stdout.replace('<', '\\\\u003c'))\n    63\t    trials = json.loads(args.composite_trials.read_text()) if args.composite_trials else []\n    68\t    temporary.write_text(page)\n     5\t   - **Idea cards and related questions.** Candidate briefs read the judgement directly. Related questions do the same. The mapping and summary calls can carry it into prose, and the browser can turn judgement history into a composite score and chart. This also matters when `/ideas` is asked to omit its bundles. Apply the release rule before composing the answer. [idea.py:137](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:137) · [idea.py:156](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:156) · [idea.py:278](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:278) · [idea.py:379](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:379) · [composite.js:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/idea/composite.js:29)\n     6\t   - **Closed questions.** §4 explicitly keeps the open/closed records. Their reason can contain the final answer. Running the existing closing-reason function read-only on `v8` produced “at rung 2 Bullish.” History and bundles return that text, and the detail page displays it. The public record can say the question closed without disclosing where it finished. [design:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:46) · [pull.py:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/pull.py:16) · [service.py:280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:280) · [bundle.py:112](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:112) · [thesis-detail.js:204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/components/thesis-detail.js:204)\n     7\t   - **Live and offline exports.** Name `/library`, `/thesis-bundles`, their MCP equivalents, the JSON export and the standalone HTML. The HTML builder accepts existing JSON and embeds it in the page. Already-prepared data can bypass both Python’s bundle builder and the JavaScript adapter. The release check must inspect the delivered data as well as the visible page. The separate timeline report and bet card also print judgements directly and should be identified as internal if excluded from release. [hivemind_api.py:205](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/hivemind_api.py:205) · [hivemind_mcp.py:96](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/hivemind_mcp.py:96) · [mock_data.py:31](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_data.py:31) · [mock_build.py:27](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:27) · [mock_build.py:61](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:61) · [prepare-data.mjs:12](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/prepare-data.mjs:12) · [report.py:42](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/report.py:42) · [card.py:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/agent/card.py:20)\n     8\t   - **Search and processing dates.** Server search can keep its ranking. Semantic search uses the possible outcomes, and its returned score measures relevance to the query. Neither uses the selected outcome. The browser library separately sorts by latest assessment date, and `record()` reads the last judgement’s day and round. Those are readers of assessment timing. Reporting zero rounds for a question with 75 would also give the reader a false fact. [search.py:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/search.py:46) · [search.py:275](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/search.py:275) · [library.js:32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/model/library.js:32) · [service.py:334](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:334) · [design:45](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:45)\n     9\t\n    10\t   **The proposed number-question rule fits the three comparison stores but fails on supported data.** I counted numeric bounds on 19/47, 17/43 and 18/49 questions in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`. On the sealed ledger used by the service tests, Data Center revenue `v3` has no `lo` or `hi` columns at all. Yet `evaluate(v3, >= $300B)` returned `holds` and the judged $300–350B range. The reverse case also exists. Stored Xbox question `v37` has explicit **Yes/No** answers with numeric bounds around zero. The current opening check accepts a ladder with every bound null. Define identity by the kind of answer the question asks for, cover both stored examples, and specify what the release does when an older record is ambiguous. The existing helper for linking questions has a narrower, asset-only purpose. [tests/test_service.py:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:18) · [tests/test_service.py:119](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:119) · [stored Xbox ledger:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md:20) · [extraction.py:493](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:493) · [links.py:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:144)\n    11\t\n    12\t3. **Faithfulness. Show the question, its sources and “Forecast unavailable.” Omit the ladder from the release answer.** The possible bands do not by themselves identify Hivemind’s choice. But Alex approved “只显示问题和来源,” and D756 says **only** those three things appear. That also settles the proposed counts and processing details on this screen. Preserve amounts quoted by sources. For `evaluate`, the unavailable verdict and removal of the judged fields are right. `claim_position` describes the caller’s amount, but repeated calls can reveal the hidden band boundaries. Omit it from the release response and give the idea card a dedicated unavailable display. Today it either falls through to a generic badge or formats a “Judged” line. [D726:10997](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10997) · [D756:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833) · [service.py:553](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:553) · [idea.js:136](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/idea/idea.js:136)\n    13\t\n    14\t4. **Switch. Fix the release setting at `withheld`.** One launcher-level choice is reasonable where release and POC share code. Pass it through HTTP, MCP, idea composition and the static build. There is no open question about the release default. The separate decision Alex could take later is whether to change what colleagues see in the existing POC. Research already reads stores directly. [design:55](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:55) · [docker-compose.yml:9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docker-compose.yml:9) · [docker-compose.yml:28](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docker-compose.yml:28) · [mock_build.py:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:20)\n    15\t\n    16\t5. **Acceptance. The proposed page check does not prove the promised screen.** `verify-page.mjs` generates a fixture and selects `v3` or the first thesis. The current UI calls an empty history “Not assessed yet,” and its schema requires at least two rungs. When Alex opens release work, use the specified `v8` with its 75 judgements and 69 change rows. Open that exact question, verify the literal marker and the same sources, and inspect the response behind the page. Include the closed-question reason and idea card in that check, with a yes/no question as the unchanged control. [design:74](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:74) · [verify-page.mjs:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/verify-page.mjs:11) · [thesis.schema.json:369](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/model/thesis.schema.json:369) · [thesis-detail.js:184](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/components/thesis-detail.js:184)\n    17\t\n    18\t**Verdict — not ready for release work.** The design would expose a forecast through the idea card and closing text, miss a known revenue question, and display more than Alex approved. Revise those contracts before implementation. This review was read-only and cost $0.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"1. **Yes. The council may open the local, $0 release build tonight.** D726 records Alex’s approval of “Forecast unavailable” and says release work had not started. Council 72 interpreted the timing as Alex’s call. Alex himself later delegated decisions to the council, then explicitly chose “结束这条线，预测暂缺上线.” Building and checking a separate package carries out that choice. It is reversible because the package can be discarded without changing what the POC serves. My round 73 vote is to open this bounded work. Once Claude agrees, record the decision under D439 before implementation. This review made no edits and ran no release check. [D726 · DECISIONS-log.md:10997](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10997) · [Alex’s delegation · DECISIONS-log.md:11658](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11658) · [Alex’s release choice · DECISIONS-log.md:11830](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11830) · [Council 72’s interpretation · DECISIONS-log.md:11844](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11844) · [D439 procedure · AGENTS.md:41](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:41)\n\n2. **Choose §4(a).** For every event or Yes/No question, show the question, its evidence, and the answer with its original label. Omit the generated explanation. One stored event explanation repeats a forecast of “around $1 trillion.” Option (b) would preserve explanations for 21 of 85 latest answers across the comparison runs, but checking only what the judge saw that day misses forecasts copied from earlier reasoning. Option (a) is cheaper and reversible. It needs no lookup of past requests, and the original explanations remain available for a later decision. The cost to readers is real: they lose the written rationale for those answers. [Known leaks · FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:27](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:27) · [Measured tradeoff · FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:93](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:93) · [Earlier reasoning passed to the judge · judging.py:211](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:211)\n\n3. **Close all three v13s checker defects as won’t-fix for the retired line.** Keep the findings and the sealed STOP result. The defects concern a parenthesized period, a change over time misread as a range, and a table number split across lines. I found `calc_small.py` callers only in research code. Alex closed the line and explicitly retained these defects for the record. Repairing its checker would change no release output, and the run rules bar tuning on these 36 answers. [Corrected findings · PAID-V13S-RESULT.md:76](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-V13S-RESULT.md:76) · [Research caller · paid_gate.py:28](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:28) · [STOP rule · PAID-GATE.md:282](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:282) · [Alex’s disposition · DECISIONS-log.md:11832](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11832)\n\n4. **Build the exporter and check the finished package first. Prove the reader’s screen second.**\n   - **First slice, $0.** Have the release builder call the Python exporter directly and accept only its output. On `old-1/v8`, verify that the package preserves the question, evidence, quoted amounts, and “Forecast unavailable.” The stored case has 75 judgements and 69 change rows, so it exercises a real forecast history. In the same test package, `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` must keep their event labels and lose the leaked forecast prose. Include an ordinary event as a control, a real closing change on a temporary copy, and an idea backed only by `v8`. Inspect the idea request using a recorded or test response. Prove the checks catch an extra field, a misclassified question, a hidden forecast read during idea composition, and foreign data in the package. [Stored cases · FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:24) · [Builder contract · FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:35](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:35) · [Tests and controls · FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:109](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:109)\n   - **Second slice, still local.** Open that package in the release UI. Verify the exact `v8` question and idea card show the same sources and marker, both events retain their labels, and the page makes zero network requests. Deliberately restoring the live `/library` fetch must fail the check. Only this slice completes Alex’s requested screen proof. [Screen requirement · DECISIONS-log.md:11835](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11835) · [Existing live fetch · bootstrap.js:256](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:256) · [Release acceptance · FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:128](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:128)\n   - **Wait for Alex** before committing, pushing, publishing, deploying, changing colleagues’ POC, or opening further paid or judge work. Both local slices fit tonight’s delegation with the existing credentials and provider caps untouched. [Authority limits · AGENTS.md:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:46) · [POC decision · FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:63](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:63) · [Paid and judge work · DECISIONS-log.md:11818](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11818)"}}
